      <LC_LandCoverClass id="24" uuid="7835e803-864b-11eb-aa79-a86daa922d76" xsi:type="LC_LandCoverClass">
         <name>Prairie</name>
         <description>Prairie is a type of vegetation cover that settles in plains dominated by grass and shrubs or woods (tree prairie) and scrub (semi-always green and semi deciduous) with less than 30% tree cover. These formations occupy regions with annual rainfall below 1200 mm. In these formations the acacias predominate;Acacia nigrescensens, Acacia xantophloea, A. nilotica, A. goetzei, which, in some cases, are associated with other xerophilic species such as Commiphora spp.</description>
         <map_code>4</map_code>
         <elements>
            <LC_HorizontalPattern id="25" uuid="7835e802-864b-11eb-aa79-a86daa922d76" xsi:type="LC_HorizontalPattern">
               <name>Horizontal Pattern 1</name>
