      <LC_LandCoverClass id="31" uuid="523b8143-864c-11eb-aa79-a86daa922d76" xsi:type="LC_LandCoverClass">
         <name>Flooded herbaceous area</name>
         <description>Wetlands comprise areas permanently or temporarily flooded with or without shrub or herbaceous vegetation. In the present classification this class was defined up to the second classification level, incorporating shrub vegetation, wetland and water body. In these areas there are marshy places, marshes, peat or water, natural or artificial, permanent or temporary, with stagnant or running water, fresh or brackish.  </description>
         <map_code>6</map_code>
         <elements>
