      <LC_LandCoverClass id="73" uuid="15567e90-6a0a-11ec-ba4e-a86daa922d76" xsi:type="LC_LandCoverClass">
         <name>Mecrusse</name>
         <description>Mecrusse is a type of vegetation that occurs in Mozambique in a gregarious way, where the main species present in its canopy is Androstachys johnsonii, belongs to the Euphorbiaceae family. This vegetation is characterized by low biological diversity and uniformity in terms of individuals, both in diameter and in height. In Mozambique it is found in Gaza, Inhambane and small patches in Nampula province.  </description>
         <map_code>12</map_code>
         <elements>
            <LC_HorizontalPattern id="74" uuid="623d1760-6a0e-11ec-ba4e-a86daa922d76" xsi:type="LC_HorizontalPattern">
